{
  "name": "GRC evidence: Okta",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "triggerAtHour": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "8f780c76-6acd-5821-b46f-96c1eb765368",
      "name": "Every day at 06:00",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "fc856ce1-ebe3-52a4-b983-861d7b40608b",
              "name": "okta_url",
              "value": "https://yourcompany.okta.com",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "946df8a9-ae73-569f-a27d-98ae610807da",
              "name": "grc_url",
              "value": "https://grc.yourcompany.example",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "1ae0a700-4cae-5116-8042-88b07fc89bde",
      "name": "Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "EDIT THESE VALUES. grc_url is the address of your GRC platform.",
      "notesInFlow": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.okta_url }}/api/v1/users?limit=200",
        "options": {
          "pagination": {
            "pagination": {
              "paginationMode": "responseContainsNextURL",
              "nextURL": "={{ ($response.headers.link || '').split(',').map(p => p.match(/<([^>]+)>;\\s*rel=\"next\"/)).filter(Boolean).map(m => m[1])[0] }}",
              "paginationCompleteWhen": "other",
              "completeExpression": "={{ !( ($response.headers.link || '').split(',').map(p => p.match(/<([^>]+)>;\\s*rel=\"next\"/)).filter(Boolean).map(m => m[1])[0]) }}",
              "limitPagesFetched": true,
              "maxRequests": 100
            }
          }
        },
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "id": "b8724860-0e3e-5e9c-b5c3-9d890cd8f865",
      "name": "Users",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        440,
        300
      ],
      "executeOnce": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.okta_url }}/api/v1/users/{{ $json.id }}/factors",
        "options": {},
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "id": "a76f8011-84c4-5280-b3dd-9b9d1b482fec",
      "name": "Factors",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        660,
        300
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One item per user, with only what the checks test. Factors arrive in the same order as users.\nconst users = $('Users').all().map(i => i.json).filter(u => u && u.id);\nif (!users.length) throw new Error('Okta returned no users. Check the address and the token.');\nconst now = Date.now(), days = s => s ? Math.floor((now - new Date(s).getTime()) / 86400000) : null;\nconst byUser = {};\nfor (const it of $input.all()) { const idx = it.pairedItem ? it.pairedItem.item : 0; (byUser[idx] = byUser[idx] || []).push(it.json); }\nconst items = users.map((u, i) => { const last = days(u.lastLogin); return { user: (u.profile || {}).login, status: u.status,\n  factors_enrolled: (byUser[i] || []).filter(f => f && f.status === 'ACTIVE').length, days_since_login: last === null ? days(u.created) : last, never_signed_in: last === null }; });\nreturn [{ json: { checks: ['okta_mfa_enrolled', 'okta_inactive_accounts'], source_ref: 'Okta ' + $('Settings').first().json.okta_url + ' (n8n)', collected_at: new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 19), items } }];"
      },
      "id": "21f3fd29-cf61-59cd-a3fc-b8a1148f7a2e",
      "name": "Shape users",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        880,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $('Settings').first().json.grc_url }}/api/integrations/collect",
        "options": {},
        "method": "POST",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}"
      },
      "id": "763ca63b-3e0a-51e2-a97e-55dbd657a3df",
      "name": "Send to GRC",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1100,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## GRC evidence: Okta\n1. Edit **Settings**.\n2. On *Users* and *Factors* choose a **Header Auth** credential: Name `Authorization`, Value `SSWS <okta api token>`. Create the token as a Read-only Administrator.\n3. On *Send to GRC* choose a **Header Auth** credential: Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer <GRC API token>` (limited to the register `evidence`).\n4. Run once with **Execute workflow**, then switch it to Active.\n\nFeeds the checks `okta_mfa_enrolled` and `okta_inactive_accounts`. Read-only.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "89ce194a-7774-55e4-9ced-ad3f04b83d18",
      "name": "Read me",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -20
      ]
    }
  ],
